   "evidence": "New signature `lemma isSpectatorSplit_pTransverse_q (g) (K) (hqq) (hTT)` has no `hSymm`, while the deleted `exists_orthogonal_spectator` took `(hSymm : g.IsSymm)` and used `hqT : g K.q T = 0 := by rw [hSymm.eq, hTq]` precisely to obtain `b = g K.q v / g K.q K.q`. The general constructor it now calls, `Bilin.isSpectatorSplit_of_gram_ne_zero`, yields `y = (g a a * g b v - g b a * g a v) / det`, which reduces to `(q\u00b7v)/(q\u00b7q)` only when `g b a = g q p_T = 0`.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/QFT/Scattering/DIS/Tensors/Basic.lean",
   "fix": "Either drop the coefficient sentence, or qualify it: \"for symmetric `g`, `p_T` and `q` are orthogonal in both slots and the coefficients are \u2026\".",
   "issue": "`isSpectatorSplit_pTransverse_q`'s docstring claims \"Since `p_T` and `q` are orthogonal, the coefficients are `a = (p_T\u00b7v) / (p_T\u00b7p_T)` and `b = (q\u00b7v) / (q\u00b7q)`\", but this PR dropped the `hSymm : g.IsSymm` argument the predecessor `exists_orthogonal_spectator` carried. Without symmetry only `g p_T q = 0` is available (`pTransverse_orthogonal_q`), not `g q p_T = 0`, so the `b` formula is false in general; it also describes the proof's witnesses rather than the statement (the coefficients are existentially bound inside `Bilin.IsSpectatorSplit.span`).",
